#: 5abf4daa657c409081889564474f90f8
msgid "**Note:** This is an important note."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:176
#: 5d446fe931cc4729a5d0aed703dec91f
msgid "Alerts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:178
#: a74506721d8d4092a2502a1de06c5e9f
msgid ""
"Alerts are sections of HTML used to draw the reader’s attention to important "
"information, such as warnings, and for stylistic purposes. They are "
"typically styled as colored text boxes, usually accompanied by icons. Alerts "
"should generally be used somewhat sparingly, so as not to cause `alert "
"fatigue <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alarm_fatigue>`__ and since they must "
"be written in HTML instead of Markdown, which makes the source less readable "
"and more difficult to work with for localization and automation purposes. "
"Here are examples of several types of alerts and their recommended icons:"
msgstr ""

