msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:227
#: 3910a3d7a512466ab12a80b94b7c0dcc
msgid "Writing command-line examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:229
#: 8ea861a9359041528c1deba292832df8
msgid "When providing command-line examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:231
#: 9f293266e76e4bc48f1eaed67832188a
msgid ""
"Tell the reader where to open a terminal (dom0 or a specific domU), and show "
"the command along with its output (if any) in a code block, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:242
#: e446b9b7d31b44c9bb2e8dad44771c9f
msgid ""
"Precede each command with the appropriate command prompt: At a minimum, the "
"prompt should contain a trailing ``#`` (for the user ``root``) or ``$`` (for "
"other users) on Linux systems and ``>`` on Windows systems, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:243
#: d45d6a4656384d9db1dfec1586e16fb6
msgid ""
"Don’t try to add comments inside the code block. For example, *don’t* do "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:256
#: b3394aaf8f4e4ac8a5c10d239417d100
msgid ""
"The ``#`` symbol preceding each comment is ambiguous with a root command "
"prompt. Instead, put your comments *outside* of the code block in normal "
"prose."
msgstr ""

